Treat each tile `i` as the middle of a group. Its left neighbour is `colors[i-1]` and its right neighbour is `colors[(i+1) % n]`, which handles the wrap-around of the circle. The group is alternating when the middle tile differs from both neighbours, so we count every `i` where that holds.

