- Scan the string from left to right.
- When we see a letter, push it onto the stack.
- When we see a digit, pop the top of the stack. That top is the nearest remaining letter to the digit's left.
- At the end, the letters left on the stack, in order, form the answer.

The input is guaranteed to allow deleting every digit, so the stack is never empty when we pop.

