        return len(word) // k - max(c.values())
```

Only the last case-conversion operation (type 2 or 3) matters. Every type-1 change made after it must survive untouched, and everything else gets converted.

The approach:
1. Find the index of the last type 2 or 3 operation.
2. Apply all type-1 operations in order. For each one, record the index of the operation that last wrote each position.
3. For each position, if it was last written before the final conversion (or never written), apply that conversion. Otherwise, leave it as is.

