A string is beautiful exactly when it can be split into consecutive pairs (positions 0-1, 2-3, 4-5, ...) where both characters in each pair are equal.

- If every pair has equal characters, each pair is a valid even-length block of a single character, so the string is beautiful.
- Conversely, in any valid partition every block has even length and starts at an even index. So each aligned pair lies entirely inside one block, and both of its characters must be equal.

So we only need to fix each aligned pair independently. A pair with two different characters needs exactly one change, and a pair with equal characters needs none.

