Treat each cell with value 1 as the corner of the right angle. The other two points must be a different 1 in the same row and a different 1 in the same column.

So first count the 1s in every row and every column. For a 1 at cell (i, j), the number of triangles with that corner is `(row[i] - 1) * (col[j] - 1)`. Summing this over all cells containing 1 gives the answer.

