For each flavor, keep track of its top two deliciousness values.

**Same flavor.** If a flavor has at least two cups, its best pair is its largest value `a` plus half of its second largest `b`. That gives a candidate of `a + b // 2`.

**Different flavors.** Take each flavor's maximum value. Sort those maxima in descending order. If there are at least two flavors, the best different-flavor pair is the sum of the two largest maxima. This is optimal because any different-flavor pair can be swapped for the maxima of those same two flavors without lowering the sum.

The answer is the larger of the two candidates. If there is only one flavor, only the same-flavor candidate exists. Since N ≥ 2, that flavor has at least two cups, so the candidate is always defined.

